{
 "format": "openchronology",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "The Great Depression, 1929–1941",
 "description": "The Great Depression in the United States and around the world: the boom of the 1920s and its cracks, the Crash of 1929 and the market's three-year fall, the banking panics, the European crisis and the end of the gold standard, the Hoover years and the Bonus Army, the Dust Bowl, Roosevelt's New Deal, the court fight and the recession of 1937–38, the culture of the decade, and the war economy that ended it.\n\n**How to read it.** Chapter headings mark the stages. Presidencies, programs, panics, droughts, recessions and the market's slide are durations; everything else is a moment, tagged by thread (market, banking, policy, politics, world, labor, farm, culture, economy). Related moments are linked: a cause and what it led to.\n\n**Dates and figures.** Local days, shown at a fixed UTC−5, New York's standard time, so the Crash's market hours read as Wall Street's. The business cycle follows the NBER's dates (to the month); unemployment rates are the Bureau of Labor Statistics' later annual estimates, placed at mid-year. Where a date or a figure is approximate, its dating note or its notes say so.\n\nA sample timeline built from the cited sources (Wikipedia, the NBER, the Bureau of Labor Statistics, the Federal Reserve's history essays, the National Archives and others); not a definitive history.",
 "presentation": {
  "mode": "gregorian",
  "unit": "",
  "scale": "1/1",
  "origin": "0/1",
  "version": 1,
  "offsetMinutes": -300,
  "significantDigits": 6
 },
 "tags": [
  "history",
  "great depression",
  "economics",
  "united states",
  "new deal",
  "education"
 ],
 "plugins": [
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "rich-text-notes",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Rich text notes",
    "description": "Edit moment and stack notes visually, storing portable Markdown. Hover cards render safe headings, emphasis, lists, code and HTTPS links. HTML and images are not executed.",
    "fields": [],
    "notes": {
     "kind": "markdown"
    },
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "moment-headings",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Headings",
    "description": "Let a moment act as a heading or marker: only its title shows, sized as a heading from level 1 to 6, and the title is what you click. Choose its font (Times New Roman by default). Headings still group into summaries with other moments.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "heading",
      "metadataKey": "headingLevel",
      "label": "Heading level"
     },
     {
      "kind": "font",
      "metadataKey": "headingFont",
      "label": "Heading font"
     }
    ],
    "marker": {
     "kind": "heading",
     "metadataKey": "headingLevel"
    },
    "targets": [
     "moments"
    ]
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "moment-sources",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Sources",
    "description": "Show and edit a series of source links for moments and stack entries.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "links",
      "metadataKey": "sources",
      "label": "Sources"
     }
    ],
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "moment-colors",
    "version": 2,
    "name": "Moment colors",
    "description": "Choose muted semantic swatches or a custom color for moments and stack entries while preserving their white borders.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "color",
      "metadataKey": "color",
      "label": "Moment color"
     }
    ],
    "marker": {
     "kind": "color",
     "metadataKey": "color"
    },
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.color(api.get(\"color\")); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "dating-context",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Dating context",
    "description": "Explain the precision and coordinate convention of a moment. An exact stored coordinate can still represent an approximate age or a calendar-day marker.",
    "fields": [
     {
      "kind": "text",
      "metadataKey": "datePrecision",
      "label": "Date precision"
     },
     {
      "kind": "multiline",
      "metadataKey": "coordinateConvention",
      "label": "Coordinate convention"
     }
    ],
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.none(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "expand-on-hover",
    "version": 1,
    "name": "Expand on hover",
    "description": "Hover or focus a summary of two to five moments to fan out its members radially for individual inspection. Larger summaries stay collapsed.",
    "fields": [],
    "summary": {
     "kind": "radial"
    },
    "source": "function render(moment: string, api: PluginAPI): string { return api.expand(); }"
   },
   "enabled": true
  },
  {
   "manifest": {
    "apiVersion": 1,
    "id": "timeline-theme",
    "version": 2,
    "name": "Timeline theme",
    "description": "Choose the timeline's colors, fonts and text sizes: its labels, its measure (the axis, tick marks and their times), the halo that keeps them readable over images, the default marker and duration colors, and a background color. Set them here in the plugin list; anything left blank keeps the usual look, and colors chosen for events still win.",
    "fields": [],
