   "metadata": {
    "title": "Unemployment peaks: 24.9%",
    "description": "**24.9%** of the civilian labor force out of work, about **12.8 million** people, in the Bureau of Labor Statistics' estimates (Stanley Lebergott's, the basis of Historical Statistics' series). No one measured unemployment directly at the time: these are later estimates, and others who count relief workers as employed put the 1930s lower. The worst year: one worker in four. More than 9,000 banks had closed since 1930.",
